      "id": "claim_d78c8e55ba14498cbafbd1363e9a5054",
      "statement": "The Defensive Frontend Principle (Story 89.4-FE) requires the frontend to indicate rather than silently transform data it doesn't own: on backend anomalies (field inversion, null-where-number, impossible negatives, missing/empty responses) render a warning indicator, preserve the raw value, and file a backend ticket — never swap fields, coerce nulls, or clamp values.",
